--[[
	SCRIPT DUMP EXPLORER  v2
	------------------------
	Scans the place for every Script / LocalScript / ModuleScript, lists them,
	shows the source, and gives you THREE ways to actually get the text out.

	HOW TO RUN
	  Studio > View > Command Bar, paste this whole file, press Enter.

	WHY v1's COPY BUTTON FAILED
	  Roblox has no clipboard API, and Studio intercepts Ctrl+C before a plugin
	  TextBox ever sees it. So the "select the text and press Ctrl+C" trick is a
	  dead end inside the GUI. v2 works around it:

	  1. EXPORT TO EDITOR  <- use this one. Writes the whole dump into real
	     ModuleScripts in ServerStorage and opens them in the Studio script
	     editor. Ctrl+A / Ctrl+C works there because it's a real code editor.
	  2. SHOW ALL IN ONE   <- loads every script into the viewer as one big
	     block, focused and pre-selected, in case Ctrl+C does work for you.
	  3. setclipboard      <- used automatically if your environment has it.
]]

